  "uprn": "200003970670",
  "decision_date": "06/04/2005",
  "description": "Conversion of house in multiple occupation to one 2-bedroom flat on the ground floor and one 3-bedroom first floor maisonette flat, incorporating new windows on the side elevation and rebuilding of the existing single storey side/rear infill extension (Chiswick House Conservation Area)\t",
  "site_name": "21",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "01/03/2005",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "W4 3DU",
  "street_name": "Ellesmere Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "05/04/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The proposal by reason of intensity, scale and layout of proposed accommodation, position of side elevation window, and the design, character and appearance of the extension, comply with policies ENV-B.1.1 (New development), H.3.4A (Houses in multiple occupation), H.3.4 (Conversion of dwelling houses to flats) of Council's UDP, 2003H.4.1 (Housing standards and guidelines), H.6.4 (Extensions and alterations), T.1.4 (Car and cycle parking facilities) and T.4.1 (Off-street parking) of Council's UDP, 2003.  The proposed conversion and replacement extension are considered to be an improvement of the existing buildings that will not affect the streetscene or the amenity of surrounding residents, whilst preserving and enhancing the Conservation Area in terms of policy ENV-B.2.2 (Conservation Areas) of the Council's UDP, 2003.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before theflats are occupied.",
    "Condition : 5 - No additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the side wall of the extension hereby approved without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - The roof area of the extension hereby permitted shall not be used as a balcony, roof garden or similar amenity area without the grant of further specific permission from the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 7 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8am to 6pm on Mondays to Friday and 9am to 1pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 8 - The use hereby permitted for conversion to two flats shall not be begun until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given."
  ],
